---
source: crates/pipdock-cli/tests/golden.rs
expression: "stdout_of(&[\"--help\"])"
---
Inspect, install, update and clean up Python packages in bulk.
Every mutating operation is previewed and snapshotted first.

Usage: pipdock [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  env          Manage environments
  list         List installed packages
  search       Fuzzy-search the local PyPI name index
  info         Show cached PyPI metadata for a package
  install      Install packages
  update       Update packages
  uninstall    Remove packages, guarded by the reverse-dependency check
  pin          Manage the per-environment pin list
  snapshot     Manage snapshots
  doctor       Engine check and environment sanity report
  health       Run Code Health (deptry / vulture / ruff) over a project folder
  audit        Check the environment against the PyPI advisory database
  pip-upgrade  Upgrade pip inside the selected environment
  engine       Show or set the configured engine
  index        Index maintenance
  tools        The isolated environment Code Health runs deptry, vulture and ruff from
  schema       Print the JSON Schema for a core type so scripts can pin against it
  self         Self-service helpers
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --env <PATH>
          Interpreter or environment directory. Defaults to the one `env use` set, else an auto-detected `.venv` in the working directory

      --engine <ENGINE>
          Override the configured engine for this invocation

          Possible values:
          - pip: `<python> -m pip`
          - uv:  `uv pip --python <python>`

      --json
          Machine-readable output: exactly one JSON document on stdout (CLI-SPEC §6).
          
          Prompts, warnings and engine output go to stderr. This said "NDJSON for streaming commands" until [VERSION], when several commands printed several documents.

  -y, --yes
          Assume the default at every prompt: a held-back package keeps its compatible version and an impossible one is skipped. Only `--strategy latest` forces

      --quiet
          Do not stream engine output to stderr. (The log file is written regardless.)

      --verbose
          Also write the log to stderr, at debug level

      --log-file <PATH>
          Also write the log to this file. The daily log in `data\logs\` is always kept

      --no-snapshot
          DANGEROUS: skip the pre-batch snapshot. CI images only; prints a warning.
          
          This is the sole documented escape from DATA-FLOW §9.2, and it exists because a throwaway CI container has nothing to roll back to.

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
